Vendored django-tagging
=======================

This app is a trimmed copy of django-tagging 0.5.1
(https://github.com/jazzband/django-tagging, release wheel
django_tagging-0.5.1-py3-none-any.whl), originally written by Jonathan
Buchanan and later maintained by Julien Fache (Fantomas42) and Jazzband.
Upstream is archived, so the website carries the code it needs. It is
distributed under the license in LICENSE.

The app label, the models, their database tables and the migrations are
unchanged, so existing databases keep working.

Local modifications:

- Removed everything the website does not use: tag clouds, usage and
  related-tag queries, model registration (registry.py, managers.py),
  generic.py, the tagged object intersection/union/related queries and
  the template tags other than tags_for_object, as well as the upstream
  test suite.
- TaggedObjectList takes the tag name from the URL, builds its queryset
  with the ORM instead of QuerySet.extra() and raw SQL, and no longer
  offers related tags.
- Accessing TagField on the model class returns the field instead of
  running a tag usage query.
- Dropped default_app_config and Python 2 leftovers; reformatted with
  black.
